# SRG-APP-000516-AU-000330  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must be configured to retain the identity of the
# original source host or device where the event occurred as part of the log
# record.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000516-AU-000330
group:           V-206512
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000366
control_rev5:    CM-6

contribution:    On a network input Splunk stamps each received event with the identity of
                 the connection it arrived on, and the application can keep that behavior
                 rather than discarding it.

governs:         inputs.conf - Configures inputs, distributed inputs such as forwarders, and file system
                 monitoring.

check:           inputs.conf [] connection_host not_equals none

external:        Whether each sending device puts its own identity in the payload, and
                 whether the name service resolves the sending address, carried by the
                 forwarders and by the network name service.
external:        Where the true origin is inside the message rather than on the connection
                 - a relayed syslog record, for example - the product STIG fix directs a
                 props.conf and transforms.conf host extraction instead; which extraction
                 is correct depends on the format each sending device emits, so it is a
                 per-source data decision (SPLK-CL-000260 fix text,
                 transforms.conf.spec:241).

citation:        Central Log Server SRG SRG-APP-000516-AU-000330 check text; SPLK-CL-000260
                 check and fix text; inputs.conf.spec:526 (connection_host =
                 [ip|dns|none]), inputs.conf.spec:60 (host), transforms.conf.spec:241
                 (DEST_KEY)
finding:         A network input is set to discard the connection's host identity, so
                 records aggregated through it do not retain the device where the event
                 occurred.
